<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Leo XIV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">born 1955</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Robert Francis Prevost</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Leo XIV, born Robert Francis Prevost in Chicago in 1955, was elected pope on 8 May 2025 after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-francis">Pope Francis</a>, becoming the first pope from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. An Augustinian friar, he spent many years as a missionary and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, of which he is also a citizen, and led the Vatican's office for bishops before his election.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-leo-xiv.jpg" alt="Pope Leo XIV" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Edgar Beltrán, The Pillar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pope_Leo_XIV_3_(3x4_cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
